{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772652606,"nonce":"6aX0YCdeeVQ77GrQ/Ql99KcOhec=","title":"Auto-save / undo history: proactive graph state persistence","message":"Currently graph state is only saved on explicit user action (Cmd+S or Save button). The isDirty flag tracks unsaved changes for UI indication but never triggers a save. Reverting to a saved version requires a full page reload.\n\n## Two approaches\n\n**Approach A — Debounced auto-save (simple)**\nTrigger a server save after N seconds of inactivity whenever isDirty is true. No local history — undo is limited to whatever React state provides (none currently). Easy to implement, covers the \"accidental refresh\" case, but does not provide undo beyond the browser session.\n\n**Approach B — Local undo ring buffer + periodic sync (correct)**\nMaintain a fixed-size ring buffer of full or diff-based GraphSpec+UIState snapshots in the frontend store. Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y navigate the ring buffer (local, instant). A background sync periodically writes the current head to the server. On page load, the server state is loaded and becomes the ring buffer tail. This preserves undo history within a session and survives refresh.\n\n## Preferred approach\nApproach B. The ring buffer can be as simple as an array of serialized state snapshots with a cursor. The main complexity is deciding what counts as an \"undoable action\" (coarse: any isDirty transition; fine: individual operations). Start coarse.\n\n## Design questions\n1. What is the max ring buffer depth? (50–100 states is reasonable)\n2. Should undo snapshots be full copies or diffs? (Full copies are simpler and memory is cheap for graph-sized state)\n3. Should the server sync write on every local snapshot or only on a timer? (Timer is safer — avoids thrashing the backend on rapid edits)\n4. Should the sync be optimistic (write and forget) or confirmed (wait for 200)?\n\n## Files likely involved\n- `web/src/stores/graphStore.ts`: add undoStack, redoStack, pushUndo(), undo(), redo()\n- `web/src/hooks/useShortcuts.ts`: bind Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y\n- Background sync: useEffect with setInterval in App.tsx or a dedicated hook","files":null}]}